# Architecture Rules

## Event System
- All cross-system interactions MUST go through `EventBus`. No direct hard dependencies between UI and physics components.
- All EventBus events MUST be strongly typed via enums/interfaces. No `any`.

## Game State Machine (FSM)
- Game lifecycle is strictly managed by `GameStateMachine`.
- Allowed transitions: `BootState` → `TutorialState` → `GameplayState` → `EndGameState`.
- No chaotic global flags (`isStarted`, `isOver`, `isWin`) outside `GameStore`.

## Bootstrap & Initialization
- `GameBootstrap` is the single entry point that initializes all services and scene components.
- Scene components must NOT use standard lifecycle methods (`onLoad`, `start`) for initialization — they have an `init()` method called by the Bootstrapper.
- Non-scene classes (services, utilities) must be plain TypeScript classes, NOT extend `cc.Component`.

## UI — MVP Pattern
- All UI implemented with Model-View-Presenter.
- `View` only handles rendering, receives scene refs via `LevelConfig`.
- `Presenter` subscribes to `EventBus`, reads `GameStore`, updates `View`.
- `View` and `Presenter` are plain TS classes initialized in `GameBootstrap`.

## Ad Network Abstraction
- All store redirects and game-ready signals MUST use `AdNetworkManager.handleClickout()` / `AdNetworkManager.gameReady()`.
- Never call `mraid.open()` or ad-network APIs directly in game components.
